# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# The repository root .gitignore is written for a Python project and has no node_modules rule, so
# without this file the first `git add js/` in this directory commits 51 installed packages. Scoped
# here rather than added to the root ignore because js/ is the only Node tree in the repository and
# the root file belongs to the Python half.
#
# package-lock.json is NOT ignored, deliberately: .github/workflows/js.yml runs `npm ci` against it
# with `cache-dependency-path: js/package-lock.json`, which needs the lockfile committed. It is also
# what makes "no CDN dependencies anywhere" checkable — every byte the tests install is pinned there
# by integrity hash.

node_modules/

# vitest / tsc scratch output. Nothing in this package emits a build: `files: ["src"]` publishes the
# sources as written, and `tsc` runs with --noEmit.
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
